# Cursor Rules for Cognitive Workbench

## Code Formatting

- Format dictionaries and action objects as single lines when the total length is less than 120 characters
- Prefer single-line format for simple action dictionaries (e.g., `{"type": "load", "target": "conversation", "out": "$conv"}`)
- Use multi-line format only when the dictionary exceeds 120 characters or improves readability significantly

## Examples

**Single-line (preferred when < 120 chars):**
```python
load_action = {"type": "load", "target": "conversation", "out": "$conv"}
```

**Multi-line (use when > 120 chars or improves readability):**
```python
load_action = {
    "type": "load",
    "target": "conversation",
    "out": "$conv",
    "additional_long_parameter": "very_long_value_that_makes_this_exceed_120_characters"
}
```
